Typical sky conditions (V-band sky brightness in mag/arcsec^2, seeing in
arcsec, extinction in mag/airmass) used as starting points for the ETC:

- Göttingen (urban): sky brightness ~19.0, seeing ~2.0", extinction ~0.25
- Sutherland, SAAO (dark site, 1760 m): sky brightness ~21.8, seeing
  ~1.2", extinction ~0.10
- McDonald Observatory, Mt Locke (dark site, 2070 m): sky brightness
  ~21.7, seeing ~1.8", extinction ~0.15

The sky magnitude is given in V; when simulating in another filter,
adjust it accordingly. Airmass is set to a typical observing value and
should be adapted to the actual observation.
